<%#
  "You're in production mode" / "Switched to …": a link brought someone from
  My into production mode, or a message or notification just switched them
  to another organization (ManageController#note_mode_switch). Soft pink,
  with Exit as a shortcut back (Tim, 2026-10-20), and it fades after a few
  seconds; with Don't ask again it's the one sign a switch happened (Tim,
  2026-10-21).
%>
<% if @switched_into_production_mode && Current.organization %>
  <div data-controller="notice" data-notice-timeout-value="5000" class="fixed inset-x-0 top-4 z-[60] flex justify-center px-4 pointer-events-none lg:pl-[272px]">
    <div data-notice-target="container" role="status"
         class="pointer-events-auto flex items-center gap-3 max-w-md w-full rounded-xl border border-pink-200 bg-pink-50 shadow-lg px-4 py-3 transition-all duration-300" data-mode-switch-notice>
      <span class="min-w-0 flex-1 text-sm text-gray-800">
        <% if @switched_to.present? %>
          Switched to <strong class="text-gray-900"><%= @switched_to %></strong>. You're in production mode.
        <% else %>
          You're in production mode for <strong class="text-gray-900"><%= Current.organization.name %></strong>.
        <% end %>
      </span>
      <%= render "shared/button", text: "Exit", variant: "secondary", size: "small", path: my_dashboard_path %>
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>
